{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 960,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Astrophysicists have discovered a black hole\nthat for millions of years has been blasting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5160,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vast particle beams in opposite directions\nacross the sky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7920,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And has recently swiveled to point its one\nof these jets directly at us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12720,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is this an intergalactic death ray of an alien\ncivilization that has suddenly noticed us?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18840,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Absolutely not, and there’s no danger whatsoever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21180,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it’s a pretty cool phenomenon anyway,\nand something we’ve never seen before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30840,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The most extreme phenomenon in the universe\nafter the Big Bang itself has to be the quasar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35940,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where a gigantic black hole at the heart of\na galaxy shreds the matter falling into it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40560,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spitting out an enormous amount of energy\nin the process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43140,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The searing whirlpools of quasars - their\naccretion disks - are so bright that they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48960,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can be seen at further distances than almost\nany other object in the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52740,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quasars are cool and all, but they’re only\none subtype of a larger category of space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58260,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "object called the active galactic nucleus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60900,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the broad name for all the different\nthings we might see when a supermassive black"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66480,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hole accrete matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67440,
    "dDurationMs": 7080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have things like Seyfert galaxies, when\nthe relatively piddling black holes in smaller,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74520,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mostly spiral galaxies start munching."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77460,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or we have radio galaxies, when the inflating\nmaterial gets spat out again in jets that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83340,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "end up blasting radio light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85140,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or we have blazars, when one of those same\njets are pointing straight at us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90060,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The different types of AGN are all related\nby a few parameters — how big the black"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95880,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hole is, how heartily the black hole is currently\nfeeding, whether it’s able to form a jet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101400,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a really big one is the orientation of\nthe system."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104520,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which way is the whole accretion disk and\njet pointing compared to us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110820,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It took us a long time to figure out that\nall these different weird looking things on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115380,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sky were different manifestations of the\nsame basic phenomenon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119340,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But once we realised that, it all made a lot\nmore sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122220,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, until AGNs of one type started turning\ninto AGNs of other types."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127260,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the weirdest example of this is \nwhen an entire AGN, gigantic black"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133380,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hole included, appears to have rotated on\nthe sky to point straight at us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138420,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see why this is so weird, let’s take\na look at what makes these different objects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142860,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what they are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143940,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the basic picture of the active galactic\nnucleus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147240,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have our supermassive black hole that can\nbe anywhere from a million to several billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152580,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times the mass of the Sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153600,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These things live in the cores of all decent "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156000,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sized galaxies, but mostly they're \nnot feeding so we can't see them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159600,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In some cases though, we have \nthe accretion disk—gas from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163320,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the surrounding galaxy that for \nsome reason has been driven into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166080,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the core and is spiraling into the black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168840,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On its way in, friction between the different\norbits heats the gas up until in glows, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174240,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "radiates light from infrared through to extreme\nultraviolet and even X-rays right near the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179820,
    "dDurationMs": 480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181080,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Surrounding the disk we think there’s a\ngiant region of very dusty material—often"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185700,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called the dusty torus—that’s fueling\nthe disk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187860,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We also have winds move material swirling\naround or being blasted out which produce"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192780,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bright spikes of light that correspond to\nspecific elements found in those winds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197880,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And sometimes those outflows are gathered\nup—“collimated”—by magnetic fields."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203100,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They’re channelled into beams of matter\nthat punch their way into the surrounding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207300,
    "dDurationMs": 240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208200,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Charged particles spiral in these magnetic\nfields, emitting synchrotron radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213060,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The energy of that radiation can be extremely\nbright in visible, ultraviolet, or even X-rays"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219000,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and gamma rays by some more exotic processes\nclose to the black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223020,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the light from the jet has lower energy\nif produced further from the black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228180,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the largest scales, when the jet has punched\nfar into the surrounding galaxy, or even into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233580,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the empty space beyond the galaxy, it shines\nas radio light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237300,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Exactly what we see when we look at one of\nthese beasts depends on a lot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242220,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But one of the most important \nfactors is orientation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244860,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the classic quasar, the accretion disk\nis fully visible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248820,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Technically quasars should also have a jet\nproducing radio emission—after all, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254400,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "word quasar comes from quasi-stellar radio\nsource, with the quasi-stellar part just meaning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260340,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it appears small - point-like to our\ntelescopes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264120,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there are also cases where you can’t see\nthe accretion disk at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267780,
    "dDurationMs": 6660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the object is aligned sort of side-on,\nthen the disk is obscured by the ring of material"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274440,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that surrounds in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275820,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then all you see is the radio jets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277920,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are radio galaxies, of which there are\nalso different types—but the coolest are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the double lobe giant radio galaxies where\nyou have thin jets of matter extending for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288360,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up to millions of light years from the galaxy\nbefore blossoming out into gigantic radio"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293520,
    "dDurationMs": 720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plumes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294240,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, if these jets are pointing along\nour line of sight rather than at right angles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300120,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to it, then we see something even weirder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302220,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can still see the accretion disk in this\ncase, but the disk’s light is faint compared"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307500,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the light from the jet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308580,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That jet contains material travelling at extreme\nvelocities—a good fraction of the speed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313920,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of light in many cases."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315780,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That causes the intensity of the jet to be\nmassively increased."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319680,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is due to the effect of Einstein’s\nspecial theory of relativity, which I can’t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324240,
    "dDurationMs": 780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explain right now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325020,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this relativistic boosting can magnify\nthe jet’s brightness by a factor of a 1000"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330360,
    "dDurationMs": 420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330780,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The result is the blazar—an AGN with extreme\nsynchrotron emission."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335220,
    "dDurationMs": 7380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Blazars are also prone to rapid flaring activity\nbecause the jet is fed by the disk unevenly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342600,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the extreme velocity of the jet speeds\nup its spluttering bursts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348000,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, to summarize, radio galaxies and blazars\ncan result from the same underlying physical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353220,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "object, with the difference only being the\nangle you observe it from."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357420,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We see radio galaxies side to size, but are\nlooking at blazars down the barrel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364200,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, can a radio galaxy turn its barrel on\nus?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368160,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well according to the very recent paper by \nLorena Hernández García and collaborators"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372360,
    "dDurationMs": 7140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that’s exactly what we're seeing in\nthe case of the poetically named PBC J2333.9-2343,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379500,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I felt I had to tell you about it \nbecause: A. It's a cool discovery and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385440,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "B. I spent a lot of my early research \ncareer thinking about Blazars and radio  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390120,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bright AGNs in general and this \nblew me away on a personal level"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395100,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so now you get to listen to \nme get all giddy about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398640,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay. This is the object in question as imaged by "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401700,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Australian Square kilometer \nArray pathfinder survey."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404520,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It may not look like much, but it is. This \nis a classic double-lobe giant radio galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411240,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The actual galaxy is right in the middle there,\nand the central supermassive black with a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416880,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mass of 250 million suns would be a dot much\nsmaller than a pixel in this image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422160,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the entire accretion \ndisk of this AGN would "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426300,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be millions of times smaller than the highest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429420,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "resolution camera that we \ncould build could ever capture."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432300,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But these radio lobes are something like a\nmillion light years from the galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437040,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To produce lobes like this, the jets from "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440400,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that central supermassive \nblack hole have to be launched"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443040,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at an angle pretty far from our own line of\nsight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445800,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Radio galaxies are thought to have jets within\n15 or so degrees of a perfect right angle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451380,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from our line of sight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452280,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that’s what we see in radio light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455160,
    "dDurationMs": 6060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the team behind this paper observed our weird\nobject all across the electromagnetic spectrum,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461220,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and at multiple times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463260,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Peering as close to the center of the galaxy "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465180,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as possible, they saw the jet \nacross the electromagnetic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468840,
    "dDurationMs": 360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spectrum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469200,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But close to the center, it wasn’t pointing\nside to side at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473460,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was pointing right at us - or at least,\nwithin 6 degrees of a bullseye in our direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478860,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In short, they saw a blazar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481800,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bright synchrotron, rapid flaring activity,\nand definitely NOT obscured by the surrounding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487440,
    "dDurationMs": 360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dust."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487800,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is completely bizarre."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490680,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those radio jets definitely aren’t pointing\nat us, but the visible and X-ray jet close"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495540,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the black hole definitely is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497880,
    "dDurationMs": 480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What gives?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498360,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe our whole story of what makes different\nAGNs different is actually wrong?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504060,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Possibly, but there’s a more likely explanation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507060,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those radio lobes were produced a long time\nago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509940,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, at least a million years ago if the\nmaterial traveled at near the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514920,
    "dDurationMs": 6180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the blazar-like jet is close to the core\n- perhaps as young as a couple thousand years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521100,
    "dDurationMs": 180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "old."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521280,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the likely answer is that the jet changed\ndirection some time between the creation of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526500,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the radio structures and the current day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528720,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it just so happens that it changed so\nthat it’s pointing directly at us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534300,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what could possibly cause such a shift?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536520,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is it even possible?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537960,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a little tricky because we don’t\nhave an exact explanation for how these jets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542640,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are launched, however we do have some plausible\nmechanisms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546960,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The jet material is very likely pulled up\nfrom the accretion disk and channeled by powerful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552420,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "magnetic fields right near the black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554580,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There isn’t much else that could do the\njob, and anyway we see jets collimated by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559620,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "magnetic fields in both young and dying stars\nand in pulsars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564060,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those magnetic fields could be locked into\nthe region just outside the black hole, or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569580,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could be connected to the inner part of the\naccretion disk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572460,
    "dDurationMs": 6300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One popular hypothesis is that to produce\na powerful jet, you need the highly ordered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578760,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and strong magnetic fields that should result\nfrom a rapidly rotating black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584760,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The jet would then be blasted out of the poles\nof that magnetic field, which would be oriented"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590580,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the black hole’s spin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592020,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if that’s the case, then to change the\ndirection of the jet you need to change the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596880,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "orientation of the entire supermassive black\nhole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600240,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More precisely, you need to change the axis\nthat the black hole is spinning around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604800,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which would take a crazy amount of energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608880,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are two ways this could happen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611040,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One is by changing the orientation of the\naccretion disk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615660,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A black hole gains its spin from the matter\nit eats."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618480,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means it tends to spin in the same direction\nas its accretion disk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623460,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But an active galactic nucleus can go through\nmultiple phases of activity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 628440,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fuel from the surrounding galaxy is driven\nto the center when the galaxy gets disturbed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633060,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in some way—typically an interaction or\na merger with another galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every time that gas falls in, it might form\na disk at a different angle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642840,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It may be that the first radio lobes were\nproduced in an ancient event that spun up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647940,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the black hole in one direction, sending jets\noff to either side."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652440,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The AGN would then have died down, but have\nbeen woken up again by a new event."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658140,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If, say, our galaxies gobbled up a smaller\ngalaxy, then the angle of that merger would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664020,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "define how the new supply of gas fell on the\ncentral black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667860,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That could be completely different angle to\nthe first accretion event."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671100,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over time, the spin of the black hole would\nhave shifted towards that new disk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675960,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second option is that a more significant\nmerger may have happened—a collision between"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681540,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two decent sized galaxies, one of which was\nour old radio galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685320,
    "dDurationMs": 6180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These galaxies would then merge and gas would\nget driven to the center to wake up the active"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691500,
    "dDurationMs": 480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nucleus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691980,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now we would have two supermassive black\nholes instead of one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695640,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These would fall together and merge, and the\nspin direction of the final black hole would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700740,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "depend on the combination of spins of the\ntwo, and also on the angle of the merger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706440,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This would most likely be different to the\ndirection of spin of either of the original"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710700,
    "dDurationMs": 780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "black holes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712140,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or maybe we’re seeing a bit of both—a\ncombination of spinning up the black hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716340,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and kicking its direction with a black hole\nmerger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718620,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However it happened, by pure chance that final\norientation has the black hole blasting its"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724320,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "jet towards us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726720,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there’s actually good evidence that\nactive galactic nuclei do change their pointing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732960,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We see radio jets that have crazy kinks in\nthem, and we have these X-shaped radio galaxies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738720,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that suggest a change in jet direction over\na very short timescale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742320,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This new guy looks like one of these things,\nbut it just so happens that the new direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747720,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is our direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749400,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, what have we learned from all of this?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751800,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, to me observations like this highlight how\ndynamic a place the universe really is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758460,
    "dDurationMs": 6540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Beyond that serene and static canvas of the\nnight sky lies a cosmos in constant and often"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765000,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "violent motion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766560,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, more pragmatically, we now have a new\nlaboratory for testing our understanding of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771660,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how astrophysical jets are made, how they’re\nconnected to their black holes, and about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775560,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the stop-start sputtering lifecycles of active\ngalactic nuclei."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780660,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And perhaps even about the crazy event that\nturned this radio galaxy into a blazar, pointing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786360,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right at us from distant parts of space time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789540,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks to everyone who supports us on Patreon. \nSupport at any level really helps give us the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794820,
    "dDurationMs": 6540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stability and freedom to keep making this show the \nway you enjoy it. Today’s special Patreon shoutout  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801360,
    "dDurationMs": 9540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "goes to Req, who’s supporting us at the big bang \nlevel. Req, just like PBC J2333.9-2343, you are as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 810900,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "brilliant as you are mysterious. Your incredible \ngravitas causes those around you to shine,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817140,
    "dDurationMs": 6540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and your luminous influence turns heads from \nacross the universe. Is the source of your blazing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823680,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "power also a swiveling supermassive black hole? \nAstrophysicists have yet to answer that question.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828660,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for now we are content to bathe in the \nrelativistic beam of your generosity. Thanks, Reg."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834600,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we recently skipped comment responses \nfor a few episodes due to my long antipodean  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840060,
    "dDurationMs": 7320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "travels. I’m now back, and the comment response \nbacklog is as long as Australia is far. Rather  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 847380,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than squeeze them all in at the end of this \nepisode, we’re going to do a livestream where  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852720,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I answer as many as possible, along with \nany questions about any topic you care to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858420,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ask during the stream—or at least, those I \ncan get to . So please join me this Monday,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 864240,
    "dDurationMs": 6900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "April 24th at 5pm eastern standard time as \nI fumble answers for your entertainment."
    } ]
  } ]
}
